 \section{Conclusion}
-A bounded solar-access screening problem can reuse exact building-level occlusion contributions while keeping its preference model and geometric limitations explicit.\aidraft{} On the frozen 45-building canonical model, all 630 pair candidates are evaluated with equivalent outputs by two same-primitive implementations. Three matched repeats yield median end-to-end times of 11,608.183~s for repeated intersection and 24.037~s for blocker reuse, including preparation. The resulting ratio is specific to those implementations and inputs.
-
-Preserved cohorts show strong same-site aggregate agreement, while controlled replays locate outside-footprint obstructions and remove the observed adverse events in four contained corrections. The results support auditable screening, not as-built accuracy, volume-matched interventions or automatic design approval. Verified boundaries, broader site coverage and additional optimized baselines are the next substantive extensions.
+\aidraft{}A bounded solar-access screening problem can reuse exact building-level occlusion contributions while keeping its preference model and geometric limitations explicit. On the frozen 45-building canonical model, all 630 pair candidates are evaluated with equivalent outputs by two same-primitive implementations. Three matched repeats yield median end-to-end times of 11,608.183~s for repeated intersection and 24.037~s for blocker reuse, including preparation. The 482.927-fold ratio compares these two unindexed, single-thread Python implementations on these inputs; it does not benchmark indexed, compiled or general-purpose solar-analysis software.
+
+Exact same-primitive A/B equivalence is distinct from the approximate cross-route agreement in the preserved same-site cohorts. Controlled replays locate outside-footprint obstructions and remove the observed adverse events in four contained corrections. The results support auditable screening, not as-built accuracy, volume-matched interventions or automatic design approval. Verified boundaries, broader site coverage and additional optimized baselines are the next substantive extensions.
 
